    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (71.52) and **Taylor Ward** (71.46) anchor our offensive effort as the clear top-tier options. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a strong combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a favorable platoon matchup against Eury P\u00e9rez, while **Taylor Ward** continues to thrive in the heart of the order, leveraging an 18% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s skill metrics to remain a must-start. **Bryson Stott** also provides excellent value at 71.06; despite a minor penalty for the opponent's ability to hold runners, his matchup against Avila\u2019s 5.01 xERA makes him a high-floor play for RBI and run production.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Gavin Sheets** (47.41), who hovered just outside the optimization threshold. While he benefits from favorable platoon splits against Emmet Sheehan, his production is heavily tethered to his spot in the lineup; the optimizer favored the higher volatility and upside of our outfield rotation, particularly the speed potential offered by **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Daulton Varsho**. We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Cal Raleigh**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Luis Arraez**; as these \"Lineup Pending\" designations resolve, any significant drop in batting order will require an immediate reassessment of their daily efficiency scores, particularly for those in the 50\u201360 range. \n\nWe continue to navigate the roster with caution regarding health, as the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** on the IL significantly limits our ceiling in power-heavy categories. While we remain aggressive on the basepaths by highlighting players like **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Masyn Winn**, and **Daulton Varsho**, we must remain diligent about our game cap management. **Jeremiah Jackson** remains a marginal play at 53.63 due to a difficult matchup against Lodolo, but with few superior alternatives currently active, he will round out the infield. The path to victory today relies on **Jonathan Aranda** capitalizing on his 0.373 xwOBA and the overall favorable platoon dynamics favoring our mid-order hitters.",
